  "description": "BULCIX crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 2/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C60 H108 Co4 Dy3 N2 O30 1+,C22 H44 Dy1 O10 1-,4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.110-3.880 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.46-111.34°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C82H160Co4Dy4N2O44. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Dy(III), Co(II), Co(III).",
